course: dictionary
lesson: 4610
title: Hiccup and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hiccup can be a noun or a verb. Its main meanings are a sudden, short "hic" sound your body makes, and, in everyday talk, a small problem or delay. Context shows you which meaning is in use.
explain: «A hiccup is the diaphragm, the big breathing muscle under the lungs, suddenly jerking while the voice box snaps shut.» The words around hiccup tell you what it means here: a body action that makes the "hic" sound.
explain: «A company whose new phone caught fire may call it "a hiccup".» The clue is caught fire. A fire is a big failure, so hiccup here means a small problem that makes a big failure sound small. Check by swapping in "a small problem": the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Look for the plural, too. «Hiccups» or «the hiccups» means having many hics one after another, as in «Dad had the hiccups all through dinner.»
fact: Hiccup can be a noun or a verb: "I have a hiccup" or "I hiccup when I eat too fast".
fact: «Hiccups» means having many short "hic" sounds one after another.
fact: In informal speech, «a hiccup» means a small problem or delay, as in «a slight hiccup in our plans».
fact: Hiccups happen when the diaphragm muscle tightens suddenly and the voice box snaps shut.
fact: «Hiccoughs» is an older spelling of hiccups, and the word can also be spelt hiccough.
exercise: «The baby got the hiccups after her milk.» What are the hiccups? | *Many short "hic" sounds one after another | A long sleep after lunch | A sore throat | A type of cough medicine
exercise: The company said its phone fire was "a hiccup". What does hiccup suggest here? | A kind of phone | A tiny, quiet sound | A big success | *A problem made to sound small
exercise: «A hiccup is the diaphragm, the big breathing muscle under the lungs.» What is the diaphragm? | *A big breathing muscle under the lungs | A kind of drink | The sound of a sneeze | A small problem
test: The trip had a slight hiccup when the bus broke down. What does hiccup mean here? | A type of bus | A happy surprise | A loud noise | *A small delay
test: Which word is a verb in «I hiccup when I eat too fast»? | fast | when | *hiccup | eat
exam: Dad had the hiccups all through dinner. What does hiccups mean here? | *Many short "hic" sounds, one after another | A small quarrel about the plates | A hot drink | A long sleep after dinner
